</ul>', '[{"id": "A", "text": "React diffs previous and new virtual DOM trees in O(N) time; the key prop provides an identity hint so React can match children across renders, avoiding destroying and re-mounting unchanged DOM nodes"}, {"id": "B", "text": "The key prop styles the HTML element with CSS"}, {"id": "C", "text": "The key prop encrypts the element text in memory"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Reconciliation deletes the entire browser document on every state change"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Medium', 100, 45, 'Direct DOM mutations are slow. React diffs in-memory lightweight JS objects (Virtual DOM). Without stable keys, adding an item at the head of a list causes React to re-render and re-instantiate every child item. Keys preserve component identity and internal state.', ARRAY['React', 'Virtual DOM', 'Reconciliation', 'Keys']::text[]);
