counter(); // 2', '[{"id": "A", "text": "A function bundled together with references to its surrounding lexical environment; it retains access to outer variables even after the outer function has executed and returned, preventing those variables from being garbage collected"}, {"id": "B", "text": "An error that closes the browser window"}, {"id": "C", "text": "A method to delete objects from RAM immediately"}, {"id": "D", "text": "A loop that terminates after 10 iterations"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Medium', 100, 45, 'Closures allow functions to maintain stateful encapsulation. Even though createCounter finished execution, counter maintains a live reference to count in its closure scope. The engine cannot garbage-collect count as long as counter is referenced.', ARRAY['JavaScript', 'Closures', 'Lexical Scope', 'Memory']::text[]);
WORKDIR /app
