', '[{"id": "A", "text": "SSE is a lightweight, one-way (server-to-client) text stream over standard HTTP/1.1 or HTTP/2, with native browser auto-reconnection and firewall compatibility; WebSockets provide heavyweight bidirectional channels"}, {"id": "B", "text": "SSE only works on Firefox"}, {"id": "C", "text": "WebSockets cannot stream text"}, {"id": "D", "text": "SSE requires UDP transport"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Medium', 100, 45, 'AI chat generation is unidirectional: the client sends a prompt once, and the LLM streams tokens back. SSE uses standard HTTP `text/event-stream` with built-in browser EventSource reconnection, avoiding WebSocket handshake and stateful proxy maintenance overhead.', ARRAY['SSE', 'Server-Sent Events', 'AI Streaming', 'WebSockets']::text[]);
const osc = ctx.createOscillator();
osc.type = ''square'';
osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(440, ctx.currentTime);
osc.connect(ctx.destination);
osc.start();', '[{"id": "A", "text": "By using the native AudioContext graph to synthesize procedural periodic waveforms (square, sawtooth, triangle waves) and shaping pitch and volume envelopes with gain nodes in real time"}, {"id": "B", "text": "By downloading MP3 files from Spotify in the background"}, {"id": "C", "text": "By reading sound bytes from GPU video memory"}, {"id": "D", "text": "By playing Windows system beep sounds"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Hard', 200, 60, 'Our Class Royale audio engine (`src/lib/sound.ts`) instantiates an AudioContext audio routing graph. An OscillatorNode generates classic arcade chiptune waveforms (square waves for lead tones, noise for explosions), completely eliminating network audio latency.', ARRAY['Web Audio API', 'Sound Synthesis', 'AudioContext', 'Frontend Engineering']::text[]);
Under the Raft Distributed Consensus algorithm (used in etcd and Kubernetes), how does the Leader Election safety invariant guarantee that a newly elected Leader contains ALL committed log entries from prior terms?', '// RequestVote RPC includes: lastLogIndex, lastLogTerm
// Candidate is voted for IF AND ONLY IF its log is at least as up-to-date as the voter''s log!', '[{"id": "A", "text": "During election, a voter rejects candidate RequestVote RPCs unless the candidate''s last log entry has a higher term, or the same term with equal/greater index; because committed entries reside on a majority of nodes and an election requires a majority vote, the candidate must possess all committed entries"}, {"id": "B", "text": "The leader reads log entries from a shared USB flash drive"}, {"id": "C", "text": "By rebooting all cluster nodes simultaneously on leader failure"}, {"id": "D", "text": "By electing the node with the fastest network card"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Boss', 500, 90, 'Raft avoids Paxos''s complex log repair during view changes. By the Quorum Intersection property, any majority of voters must contain at least one node holding the most recent committed log entry. Since that node only votes for candidates whose log is at least as up-to-date, uncommitted candidates cannot win.', ARRAY['Raft Consensus', 'Distributed Systems', 'etcd', 'Kubernetes', 'Boss Challenge']::text[]);
In a microservices Service Mesh (Istio / Linkerd), how does transparent mutual TLS (mTLS) with SPIFFE identity verification secure inter-service communication against network eavesdropping and impersonation?', NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Envoy sidecar proxies intercept all ingress and egress network traffic via iptables; the mesh control plane provisions short-lived X.509 certificates encoding SPIFFE IDs (e.g. spiffe://cluster.local/ns/prod/sa/order-service) into SAN extensions, enforcing mutual cryptographic handshake and zero-trust authorization policies at both endpoints"}, {"id": "B", "text": "By encrypting database passwords with base64"}, {"id": "C", "text": "By disabling foreign keys in PostgreSQL"}, {"id": "D", "text": "By routing traffic through public VPN servers"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Boss', 500, 90, 'Zero Trust assumes the internal network is compromised. Envoy proxies intercept sockets at the pod boundary, authenticate peers via mutual X.509 certificates minted by SPIRE/Citadel, verify cryptographically validated SPIFFE identity SANs, and enforce fine-grained L7 AuthorizationPolicies.', ARRAY['Service Mesh', 'mTLS', 'SPIFFE', 'Zero Trust', 'DevOps', 'Boss Challenge']::text[]);